From: baseband lane
Subject: 0520 pandora_mpss: cross each image with each PAS id (the first probe conflated two failures)

0510's probe sent the DTB's metadata for nine candidate ids and every one came back 0xffcfffbb,
which was read as "the id is not the problem".  That reading is unsound: it sent ONE image's
metadata to every id, so two different failures look identical --

  * the id is unknown to the secure world, or
  * the id exists but the metadata does not describe that id's image (TrustZone comparing the
    hash against the image it expects).

0520 asks four questions instead, each image with its own metadata:

    (modem_dtb.mdt, pas 0x26)   the path the ladder uses
    (modem_dtb.mdt, pas 4)
    (modem.mdt,     pas 4)      the main image with its own metadata
    (modem.mdt,     pas 0x26)

Both blobs are the tail-copy branch of qcom_mdt_read_metadata(): for modem.mdt
ehdr 948 + hash 6304 = 7252 == file size, and for modem_dtb.mdt 148 + 3896 = 4044 == file size, which
was verified against the files themselves (.temp/modem.mdt, .temp/modem_dtb.mdt).

Off by default; pandora_mpss_pas_probe2=1 enables it.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
index b0205e1..a269ff3 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
@@ -897,10 +897,49 @@ mp_probe_pas_ids(void)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * Cross the two images with the two PAS ids, each image with its OWN metadata.
+ *
+ * The first probe (0510) sent the DTB's metadata for all nine candidate ids, so its "every id is
+ * refused" result cannot separate two very different failures:
+ *   - the id is unknown to TrustZone, or
+ *   - the id exists but the metadata does not describe that id's image.
+ * TrustZone may well compare the metadata's hash against the image it expects for a given id, and
+ * a DTB blob sent for the main image's id would then be refused for the second reason while looking
+ * exactly like the first.
+ *
+ * 0520 therefore asks four questions in one boot:
+ *     (modem_dtb.mdt, pas 0x26)   the path the ladder actually uses
+ *     (modem_dtb.mdt, pas 4)
+ *     (modem.mdt,     pas 4)      the main image with its own metadata
+ *     (modem.mdt,     pas 0x26)
+ * Off by default; pandora_mpss_pas_probe2=1 enables it.
+ */
+static void
+mp_probe_cross(void)
+{
+	static const char *const images[] = { "modem_dtb", "modem" };
+	static const unsigned ids[] = { MP_PAS, MP_PAS_DTB };
+
+	if (!mp_option("pandora_mpss_pas_probe2")) {
+		return;
+	}
+	printf("PANDORA MPSS: crossing 2 images with 2 PAS ids, each with its own metadata\n");
+	for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(images) / sizeof(images[0]); i++) {
+		for (unsigned j = 0; j < sizeof(ids) / sizeof(ids[0]); j++) {
+			uint64_t answer = 0;
+			int err = pandora_pas_init_only(MP_FW_PART, images[i], ids[j], &answer);
+			printf("PANDORA MPSS: %s.mdt -> pas %u: %s (a0 %#llx)\n", images[i], ids[j],
+			    err ? "no call" : (answer ? "refused" : "ACCEPTED"), answer);
+		}
+	}
+}
+
 static bool
 step_dtb(void)
 {
 	mp_probe_pas_ids();
+	mp_probe_cross();
 	if (!mp_assign_dsm()) {
 		printf("PANDORA MPSS: the DSM regions were not assigned; continuing anyway\n");
 	}
